keywords:
  - GNSS
  - variometric approach
  - seismogeodesy
  - real-time
  - displacement
  - Julia
abstract: >-
  GaiaVario is a variometric GNSS displacement engine: for every satellite
  seen at two consecutive epochs it differences the carrier phase minus the
  modelled terms (broadcast orbit and clock, Sagnac, troposphere, solid Earth
  tide, phase wind-up) and solves the station displacement over the pair by
  weighted least squares with per-satellite rejection. It is the default
  engine plug-in of the GaiaSeis platform (interface GaiaSeisEngineAPI).
  Developed within the TRANSFORM² project (European Union, project number
  101188365).
